{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>לנידה</b> — for derision, like מנוד ראש (head-shaking), and נוד שפתי (lip-quivering), and it is from the root of נע ונד (wandering and roaming)." "<b>הזילוה</b> — the opposite of honor, like להוציא יקר מזולל (to bring forth precious from worthless), except it is from a different root. Or its meaning: they brought her down, or they made it so that her tear would flow."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:22.400940043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}